# What a module loaded through the real loader draws: a window of retained text and fills over a backdrop window, then closed.
# The same steps are the single source of truth for the native module test (docs/FIRST-WINDOW.md, "Retained fills and text").
desk-scenario 1
screen 640 480
depths 8 4
open notes 40 40 260 140 "Notes"
label notes 12 12 "A window behind the module's."
pointer 600 440
# The module's window: a 320 x 160 content area under the 22-pixel title bar and its 1-pixel rule, centred on the screen.
open hellowin 160 148 320 183 "HELLOWIN.DMD"
# The overhang at the top-left is drawn first, so the text and swatches paint over anything it shares with them; it shows as a small
# tab at the corner, clipped to the content area.
fill hellowin -10 -10 30 20 Halo2
text hellowin 8 8 Text "Drawn by HELLOWIN.DMD"
text hellowin 8 28 TextSecondary "a loaded module, through three services"
text hellowin 8 48 TextMuted "desk_window_new, desk_fill, desk_text"
fill hellowin 8 76 28 20 Raised
fill hellowin 44 76 28 20 Line
fill hellowin 80 76 28 20 Border
fill hellowin 116 76 28 20 TextMuted
fill hellowin 152 76 28 20 TextSecondary
fill hellowin 188 76 28 20 Text
fill hellowin 224 76 28 20 Accent
fill hellowin 260 76 28 20 Selection
# The overhang at the bottom-right.
fill hellowin 250 110 200 200 Accent
frame drawn
close hellowin
frame closed
